rNameEn":"House of Commons","LatestBillEventChamberNameFr":"Chambre des communes","LatestBillEventChamberName":"House of Commons","LatestBillEventNumberOfAmendments":0,"LatestBillEventAmendmentNoteId":0,"LatestBillEventMeetingNumber":"169","LatestBillEventAdditionalInformationEn":"","LatestBillEventAdditionalInformationFr":"","LatestBillEventAdditionalInformation":"","PassedHouseFirstReadingDateTime":"2026-11-18T15:11:52.61","PassedHouseSecondReadingDateTime":"2026-11-20T12:18:14.31","PassedHouseThirdReadingDateTime":null,"PassedSenateFirstReadingDateTime":null,"PassedSenateSecondReadingDateTime":null,"PassedSenateThirdReadingDateTime":null,"ReceivedRoyalAssentDateTime":null,"DidReinstateFromPreviousSession":false,"ReinstatedFromBillDocumentId":null,"ReinstatedFromBillNumberCode":null,"DidReinstateInNextSession":false,"ReinstatedAsBillDocumentId":null,"ReinstatedAsBillNumberCode":null,"PassedFirstChamberFirstReading":true,"PassedFirstChamberSecondReading":true,"PassedFirstChamberThirdReading":false,"PassedSecondChamberFirstReading":false,"PassedSecondChamberSecondReading":false,"PassedSecondChamberThirdReading":false,"ReceivedRoyalAssent":false,"ConsideredDuringPreviousSitting":true,"IsProForma":false,"BillFormId":10,"BillFormNameEn":"Regular","BillFormNameFr":"Ordinaire","BillFormName":"Regular","NotesEn":"","NotesFr":"","Notes":"","ShortLegislativeSummaryEn":"<div>The Library of Parliament does not prepare Legislative Summaries for self-explanatory measures. The following is a short summary:<br/><br/>On 18 November 2026, the Minister of Housing and Infrastructure and Minister responsible for Pacific Economic Development Canada introduced Bill C-42, An Act respecting certain measures related to affordability and housing (Grocery and Housing Affordability Act) in the House of Commons and it was given first reading.   <br/><br/>Bill C-42 amends the Income Tax Act to increase the maximum annual Canada Groceries and Essentials Benefit amounts by 50?% for the 2026-2027 benefit year. It also provides for the repeal of the Prohibition on the Purchase of Residential Property by Non-Canadians Act on 1 January 2029, and makes related amendments to the Budget Implementation Act, 2022, No. 1 and the Prohibition on the Purchase of Residential Property by Non-Canadians Regulations.</div>","ShortLegislativeSummaryFr":"<div>La Bibliothèque du Parlement ne prépare pas de Résumés législatifs pour les mesures qui sont suffisamment explicites. Ce qui suit est un court résumé :<br/><br/>Le 18 novembre 2026, le ministre du Logement et de l’Infrastructure et ministre responsable de Développement économique Canada pour le Pacifique a déposé le projet de loi C-42, Loi visant certaines mesures liées à l'abordabilité et au logement (Loi sur l'abordabilité des produits d'épicerie et du logement) à la Chambre des communes en première lecture. <br/><br/>Le projet de loi C-42 modifie la Loi de l’impôt sur le revenu afin d’augmenter les montants annuels maximaux de l’allocation canadienne pour l’épicerie et les besoins essentiels de 50?% pour l’année de prestations 2026-2027. Il prévoit également l’abrogation de la Loi sur l’interdiction d’achat d’immeubles résidentiels par des non-Canadiens le 1er janvier 2029, et apporte des modifications connexes à la Loi no 1 d’exécution du budget de 2022 et au Règlement sur l’interdiction d’achat d’immeubles résidentiels par des non-Canadiens.</div>","ShortLegislativeSummary":"<div>The Library of Parliament does not prepare Legislative Summaries for self-explanatory measures. The following is a short summary:<br/><br/>On 18 November 2026, the Minister of Housing and Infrastructure and Minister responsible for Pacific Economic Development Canada introduced Bill C-42, An Act respecting certain measures related to affordability and housing (Grocery and Housing Affordability Act) in the House of Commons and it was given first reading.   <br/><br/>Bill C-42 amends the Income Tax Act to increase the maximum annual Canada Groceries and Essentials Benefit amounts by 50?% for the 2026-2027 benefit year. It also provides for the repeal of the Prohibition on the Purchase of Residential Property by Non-Canadians Act on 1 January 2029, and makes related amendments to the Budget Implementation Act, 2022, No. 1 and the Prohibition on the Purchase of Residential Property by Non-Canadians Regulations.</div>","IsFullLegislativeSummaryAvailable":false,"StatuteYear":null,"StatuteChapter":null,"BillStages":{"BillId":0,"HouseBillStages":[{"BillStageId":60029,"BillStageNameEn":"First reading","BillStageNameFr":"Première lecture","BillStageName":"First reading","ChamberOrganizationId":1,"ParliamentNumber":45,"SessionNumber":1,"State":4,"StateNameEn":"Completed","StateNameFr":"Terminée","StateAsOfDate":"2026-11-18T15:11:52.61","StateName":"Completed","Committee":null,"Sittings":[{"NameEn":"Introduction and first reading","NameFr":"Dépôt et première lecture","Name":"Introduction and first reading","Number":"167","Date":"2026-11-18T00:00:00","AdditionalInformationEn":null,"AdditionalInformationFr":null,"AdditionalInformation":null,"IsPublished":true}],"Decisions":[],"CommitteeMeetings":[],"SignificantEvents":[{"EventTypeId":60110,"BillDocumentId":0,"EventNameEn":"Introduction and first reading","EventNameFr":"Dépôt et première lecture","EventName":"Introduction and first reading","EventDateTime":"2026-11-18T00:00:00","IsCompletionOfBillStage":true,"IsDefeatedEvent":false,"CommitteeReportId":null,"CommitteeReportNumber":null,"AdditionalInformationEn":"","AdditionalInformationFr":"","AdditionalInformation":"","MeetingEventId":null,"AmendmentNoteId":null}],"EndOfStageEvent":{"EventTypeId":60110,"EventTypeNameEn":"Introduction and first reading","EventTypeNameFr":"Dépôt et première lecture","EventTypeName":"Introduction and first reading","EventStartDateTime":"2026-11-18T15:11:52.61","EventEndDateTime":"2026-11-18T15:11:52.61"},"StageEventCount":1,"LastStageEventStartDateTime":"2026-11-18T15:11:52.61","Speeche